Error-based Attack
Attack Principle: Construct special SQL statements to trigger database errors and extract data through error messages
Feature Detection:
Type conversion errors:
Forced type conversion: CAST(... AS ...), CONVERT(...) for incompatible types
Implicit type conversion: string-number operations, aggregate functions applied to wrong types
Mathematical operation errors:
Division by zero: 1/0, MOD(x,0)
Function domain errors: LOG(0), SQRT(-1)
Numeric overflow: EXP(710), POW(9999,9999)
String function parameter errors:
SUBSTRING(str, -1), LEFT(str, -1)
EXTRACTVALUE(), UPDATEXML() with XPath errors
Date function parameter errors:
DATE_ADD(), DATE_SUB() with illegal parameters
Special error functions:
EXTRACTVALUE(1, CONCAT(0x7e, (SELECT ...)))
UPDATEXML(1, CONCAT(0x7e, (SELECT ...)), 1)
EXP(~(SELECT * FROM (SELECT ...)x))
Judgment Point: Whether these error constructions are deliberate and have no business meaning